body:
Quite a bit to follow and dig into, but thanks for the detailed presentation as it's important stuff to understand. I get the issue now, and I agree that #118080 should not be reverted (that would be worse).

However the canvas_item issue you found is also a bug which will cause inconsistent behaviour and prevent a position change from propagating when it should. Should we fix that?

I know it's risky to fix bugs like this, but this canvas_item bug wasted my time, your time, and the original developer's time because it made expected behaviour look rare and unusual and different to 3D.

What was wrong with this commented out `p_node->xform_change.in_list() &&`? It looks like it fixes the canvas_item bug you mentioned.

```diff
-	if (/*p_node->xform_change.in_list() &&*/ p_node->_is_global_invalid()) {

+	if (p_node->xform_change.in_list() && p_node->_is_global_invalid()) {
		return; //nothing to do
	}

	p_node->_set_global_invalid(true);

	if (p_node->notify_transform && !p_node->xform_change.in_list()) {
		if (!p_node->block_transform_notify) {
			if (p_node->is_inside_tree()) {
				if (is_accessible_from_caller_thread()) {
					p_node->_set_global_invalid(true);

```
